@startuml
title C6 Zitadel token -> FastAPI -> OpenFGA ListObjects -> SPARQL graph scope
actor User
participant "Zitadel" as Z
participant "FastAPI Depends" as API
participant "OpenFGA" as FGA
participant "Policy port (rdf-persistence)" as PEP
participant "SPARQL store" as ST
User -> Z : OIDC login (PKCE)
Z --> User : access token (JWT only if configured; roles claim on request)
User -> API : request + Bearer
API -> API : verify via JWKS (Authlib/PyJWT) or introspection (opaque)
API -> FGA : ListObjects(user, can_read, type graph)
FGA --> API : graph ids (capped at 1000, partial on 3s deadline, no flag)
API -> PEP : scope = set of graph IRIs
PEP -> ST : SELECT/CONSTRUCT ... FROM NAMED / VALUES ?g, also for COUNT and get-by-IRI
ST --> API : rows only from permitted graphs
note over PEP, ST : Leak trap: counts, single-item lookups and GROUP BY rows must carry the same scope
@enduml
